<title>USA: Regency Realty buys four shopping centers.</title>
<headline>Regency Realty buys four shopping centers.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla. 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Regency Realty Corp said on Tuesday it bought four shopping centers, anchored by grocery stores, for a total of $37.2 million.</p>
<p>The four properties, with a total of 467,360 square feet, were University Collection, in Tampa, Florida, Old St. Augustine Plaza in Jacksonville, Wellington Town Square in West Palm Beach, Fla. and Woodcroft Shopping Center in Raleigh, N.C. The average occupancy rate was 97.2 percent.</p>
